<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Donation of Pepin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/756">756</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/8th-century">8th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Donation of Pepin was the grant by the Frankish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pepin-the-short">Pepin the Short</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/papacy">papacy</a> of lands in central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a> taken from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombards</a>, promised in 754 and carried out in 756. It gave the popes the former <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/exarchate-of-ravenna">Byzantine Exarchate of Ravenna</a> and other territories, forming the legal basis of the Papal States, and sealed the alliance between the papacy and the Frankish kings.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/donation-of-pepin.jpg" alt="Donation of Pepin" width="320" height="308" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: English: A fresco painter from the school of Giovan Battista Ricci (c. 1537–1627); by the time the fresco was created... · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:La_donacion_de_Pipino_el_Breve_al_Papa_Esteban_II.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
